@.str.35 = private unnamed_addr constant [891 x i8] c"\0A\0A# Examples\0A\0A* Open the Nix expression of the GNU Hello package:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix edit nixpkgs#hello\0A  ```\0A\0A* Get the filename and line number used by `nix edit`:\0A\0A  ```console\0A  # nix eval --raw nixpkgs#hello.meta.position\0A  /nix/store/fvafw0gvwayzdan642wrv84pzm5bgpmy-source/pkgs/applications/misc/hello/default.nix:15\0A  ```\0A\0A# Description\0A\0AThis command opens the Nix expression of a derivation in an\0Aeditor. The filename and line number of the derivation are taken from\0Aits `meta.position` attribute. Nixpkgs' `stdenv.mkDerivation` sets\0Athis attribute to the location of the definition of the\0A`meta.description`, `version` or `name` derivation attributes.\0A\0AThe editor to invoke is specified by the `EDITOR` environment\0Avariable. It defaults to `cat`. If the editor is `emacs`, `nano`,\0A`vim` or `kak`, it is passed the line number of the derivation using\0Athe argument `+<lineno>`.\0A\0A\00", align 1
